From abb8b3809fb7054079741fdfd965e5181535b477 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: riverosmejia <riverosmejia@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:28:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] feat(tui): paths in an answer are links (port of
 quick-peek's paths)

A path the model names in prose that resolves to a real file becomes a Link:
the renderer's hover highlight is the affordance, and a click copies
`path:line` to the clipboard (wl-copy/xclip/pbcopy), or runs the user's
PEEK_OPEN template.

- lib/paths.ts: pathsIn/pathOfSpan/lineOf/resolvePath ported from midudev's
  quick-peek (MIT), plus existingPaths() with a stat cache (30s found / 3s
  missing) and a `hermes-peek://` URL builder.
- openExternalUrl: accepts only that scheme, and only for a path that exists
  here, so a `file://` the model wrote itself stays refused.
- markdown: the two plain-text pushes in MdInline go through renderProse.
- 11 tests, the original's cases among them.
